From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Composition expressions (6050)

Expression animations were kept but not evaluated, and expression key
frames other than this.StartingValue held the previous value. Programs
tie visuals together with them (a header following a scroller, a shadow
following its element, opacity from a property set).

New expression.c parses an expression once and evaluates it: numbers,
booleans, parameters, this.StartingValue/CurrentValue/FinalValue,
this.Target and reference parameters' properties (another visual's
Offset, a property set's entry) with components, unary and binary
arithmetic, comparisons, && ||, ?:, and the common functions (Vector2/3/4,
Quaternion, ColorRgb, Abs, Clamp, Lerp, Min, Max, Mod, Pow, Sqrt, Sin...,
Length, Distance, Normalize, Scale, Slerp, CreateFromAxisAngle). An
expression animation is evaluated at every step with the parameters it
had when started until stopped or replaced; references' properties are
found through their StartAnimation with an internal animation that only
asks. Expression key frames are evaluated when their animation starts;
malformed ones are refused.
